===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|домъ||ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|ru|:inh|orv:домъ}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|домъ|t=house; home}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*dȍmъ|t=house; home}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-bsl-pro|*damús}}, from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*dṓm|t=home; house}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-дом.ogg}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush-дом.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush (Reda Kerbouche)-дом.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}
* {{rhymes|ru|om|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|c||(1)|or|e|pltail=*|par=+|loc=+|adj=дома́шний,домово́й,домо́вый|dim=до́мик,домо́к,дому́шка|aug=доми́ще,доми́на|pej=доми́шко}}

# [[house]], [[building]] {{gloss|a residential building}}
#: {{syn|ru|зда́ние|q=building in general}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[обы́скивать]] '''дом''' [[за]] '''до́мом'''|to search '''house''' by '''house'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[кварти́рный]] '''дом'''|apartment '''building'''; '''block''' of flats}}
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1842|author=w:ru:Николай Гоголь<t:{{w|Nikolai Gogol}}>|title=w:ru:Мёртвые души|chapter=s:ru:[[Мёртвые_души_(Гоголь)/Том_I/Глава_VI|Том I, Глава VI]]|location=|publisher=|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:en:Constance Garnett|title2=s:en:[[Dead Souls—A Poem/Book One/Chapter VI|Dead Souls—A Poem]]|location2=London|publisher2=Chatto & Windus|year2=1922|page2=|pageurl2=
|text=Сде́лав оди́н и́ли два поворо́та, геро́й наш очути́лся наконе́ц пе́ред са́мым '''до́мом''', кото́рый показа́лся тепе́рь ещё печа́льнее.|t=After turning round two or three corners, our hero found himself at last in front of the '''house''', which looked even gloomier at close quarters.}}
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1930|author=w:ru:Нина Берберова<t:{{w|Nina Berberova}}>|title=Последние и первые|chapter=III|location=Paris|publisher=Jacques Povolozky & Cie|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:Marian Schwartz|title2=The Last and the First|location2=London|publisher2=w:Pushkin Press|year2=2021|page2=|pageurl2=
|text='''Дом''' име́л тот немно́го неве́рный вид, како́й быва́ет, когда́ там, внутри́, спят лю́ди.|t=The '''house''' had that slightly uncertain look that can happen when there are people sleeping inside.}}
# [[house]], [[home]] {{q|as part of a name of an establishment}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[изда́тельский]] '''дом'''|publishing '''house'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[сумасше́дший '''дом''']] / [[дур'''до́м''']]|insane '''asylum'''; mad'''house'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''дом''' [[отдых|о́тдыха]]|holiday '''resort'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''дом''' [[престарелый|престаре́лых]]|retirement '''home'''}}
# [[plot]] {{gloss|in some street addresses: a group of buildings sharing the same street number}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[московский|Моско́вское]] [[шоссе́]], '''дом''' 123, [[ко́рпус]] 2, [[кварти́ра]] 10|123 Moskovskoye highway, building 2, apartment 10}}
# [[home]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[родно́й]] '''дом'''|native '''home'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''Дом''' [[англичанин|англича́нина]] — [[его́]] [[кре́пость]].|An Englishman's '''home''' is his castle.}}
# [[dynasty]], [[noble]] [[house]]
#: {{uxi|ru|'''дом''' [[Романов|Рома́новых]]|the Romanov '''dynasty'''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[чума́]] [[на]] [[о́ба]] [[ваш|ва́ши]] '''до́ма'''|a plague on both your '''houses'''}}

====Usage notes====
* The nominative-accusative plural {{m|ru|до́мы}}, largely unused now, was in earlier Russian (as late as 19th century) sometimes restricted to the accusative case and distinguished from a nominative plural {{m|ru|дома́}}. Compare the nominative plural {{m|cu|домовє}}, accusative plural {{m|cu|домꙑ}} of Old Church Slavonic {{m|cu|домъ}}.

